title The cellar said what it held and never that the bytes were the bytes
prompt autonomous loop, Copal seat -- the aether lap
rota lap 4505, row 0 -- Aether, the row that hears; the row asks why the work exists, and the crossing page it seats says the strand this lap stands on, the content address is the wall
think Cold roster opened at 220 run, 218 green, 0 red, 2 gated at %5, tree_moved=no. I held still for its 41 minutes rather than void it.
think Aether listens for what a document keeps repeating. The grain page repeats one line about my own lane -- a crossing is proven by its digest, never by its header -- and foundations/20260703-202312_the-marked-value.md states the manifest line's three fields as its type-mark, its digest, and its name, with the vow the digest is checked twice.
think bron-resins/manifest.bron carried two of the three. Names and notes went whole on 20260906 after a measurement; the digest field the same law names was never added, and its own first line still read working-tier SHA3-256 names when sealed; plain paths today.
think Measured before building rather than after: every resin in the room has exactly one commit in the tree's whole history, and its blob there is byte-identical to its blob at HEAD, checked one file at a time. So the seals I recorded are the seals of the bytes that LANDED, rather than of bytes that merely stand here today.
think The refusal was shown on the REAL room before the repair -- the new gate answered unsealed=17, verdict=drifted, and named all seventeen. Then the seal lines lifted it.
obs unsealed GATES where its sibling noteless_entries only reports, and the parting is deliberate: a bare name is a weak claim about a resin, an absent seal is no claim at all, and a wall with a gap is a wall somebody walks around.
obs The instrument found its own blind spot while I used it. The scan resolved sha3.sh from its own directory, and the control copies the scan into a pen to prove the pen innocent -- so the innocence leg answered misread and proved nothing. An upward walk with the caller's root as a named fallback is the repair, and the failing leg is what named the case.
obs A SIBLING GUARD WENT FALSE AND I MEASURED IT RATHER THAN PREDICTING IT. sealed_digest asks whether a recorded digest is ever compared to its bytes, and its proxy was does a file under tools/ SPELL this digest. Seventeen digests recomputed every lap by a rostered witness spell nowhere: it answered unread=17 against a gate of zero. A WALL READ AS A SILENCE is the dangerous direction for a proxy to fail in.
obs The repair reads a second mechanism apart rather than folding it in -- read_generically, reported beside the gate, since a number that quietly absorbs a second mechanism is a number nobody can audit. Three conditions, none satisfiable by prose: a declared witness path under tools/, that file existing, and the standing roster carrying it. Each planted and lifted separately, so no one of them can pass for the whole test.
obs No red booked. The cellar was unsealed rather than wrong, and the sibling proxy never shipped a false green -- my own lap is what would have made it false, and it is repaired in the same lap.
